  "verbalization": "Gramideoxybenzoin H appears to have a shared target of SNU-387, which is involved in the replication of viral RNA. This relationship is supported by multiple evidence paths, all of which indicate that SNU-387 is a target of Gramideoxybenzoin H and is itself a target of various compounds, including a hydroxybenzoquinone derivative and a complex ester. These compounds are all implicated in the replication of the replicase polyprotein 1ab, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Gramideoxybenzoin H may inhibit viral replication. The evidence suggests that Gramideoxybenzoin H acts through a pathway that involves the modulation of SNU-387, which in turn affects the replicase polyprotein 1ab. The integration of these paths highlights a possible dependency on SNU-387 as a key mediator in the interaction between Gramideoxybenzoin H and the replicase polyprotein 1ab, reinforcing the notion that the relationship is rooted in a shared biological function.",
